@preamble use("random")
seed
@unchecked
Seeds the pseudo-random number generator with the given integer.
Using the same seed produces the same sequence of pseudo-random values.

seed(n)

seed(42)
===
random
@unchecked
Returns a pseudo-random integer n satisfying 0 <= n < max.
max must be a positive integer.
Successive calls advance the generator state; seed establishes a new
deterministic sequence.

random(max)

seed(42)
random(10)    # an integer from 0 through 9
random(10)    # an integer from 0 through 9
